# Every step of .github/workflows/windows.yml, replayed on this machine, 2026-11-28.
#
# The workflow has never run on a runner, and the Vulkan step only failed there
# because its own commands had not been run here. This pass runs each step as
# written, with the runner's conditions where they differ from this machine:
#
#   CPU_ONLY=1              the job's own env, applied to every step
#   no CUDA on PATH         for the steps that run before the toolkit is installed
#                           (the reference and CPU-shim steps), emulated by dropping
#                           every CUDA directory from PATH and clearing CUDACXX
#   a clean build directory  a runner has no build/ tree; the ONNX step was run
#                           twice for that reason, once against the stale tree and
#                           once from scratch
#   CUDA 13.0 / Vulkan SDK   this machine has both, so the toolkit preflight and the
#                           nvcc step ran against 13.0 rather than the action's
#                           12.9.1, and the Vulkan step was forced OFF as written
#
# What it found: the CUDA template did not compile with CPU_ONLY=1 at all -
# RenderFacts() called DeviceMemoryFreeBytes(), whose declaration lives inside
# Kernel.cuh's OFXPLUGIN_WITH_CUDA block, so the CPU-shim build stopped at
# "error C3861: DeviceMemoryFreeBytes: identifier not found" and the step after it
# failed for want of a bundle. That step is the fourth one in the job, so the first
# CI run would have stopped there. Fixed by compiling the fact-gathering with the
# path it serves; the counts and the suite are then as below.
#
# Not covered by this replay: setup-python 3.12 (this machine has 3.10), the two
# actions themselves (checkout, onnx-runtime), and the OpenCL step's "no device"
# branch, because this machine has an OpenCL device - its exit-2 mapping stays the
# stub measurement it was.

